    hz_t: 'Guides', hz_u: 'Short explanations of what Binderplan does. Ctrl + / opens this list anywhere.',
    hz_ph: 'Search …', hz_zurueck: 'All guides', hz_alle: 'See all guides',
    hz_nichts: 'No guide for that yet. Write to us and we will add it.',
    hz_start_t: 'Create your first binder', hz_start_u: 'Master set, Pokédex or empty – and how the first card lands in a slot.',
    hz_start_1: 'Tap the binder name at the top and choose „Create a new binder".',
    hz_start_2: 'Pick a template: a whole set, every card of one Pokémon, the Pokédex – or empty.',
    hz_start_3: 'Set the grid (2×2 up to 5×5) so the pages match your real binder.',
    hz_start_4: 'Done. Saving happens by itself; without an account the binder lives in this browser, with one it follows you.',
    hz_suchen_t: 'Find cards', hz_suchen_u: 'Name, number, set, rarity, illustrator – and what the filters can do.',
    hz_suchen_1: '„Search cards" opens the drawer next to the binder.',
    hz_suchen_2: 'Type the name, or the number like 025/165. One click on a result puts it in the next free slot.',
    hz_suchen_3: 'Filters on the left: era, set, rarity, type, illustrator, tournament mark.',
    hz_suchen_4: 'Several cards at once: „To the tray" collects them, „Insert" places them together.',
    hz_ordnen_t: 'Arrange slots', hz_ordnen_u: 'Drag, swap, push, select – and undo all of it.',
    hz_ordnen_1: 'Dragging a slot moves the card. The „Swap/Push" button decides what happens to the others.',
    hz_ordnen_2: 'Swap exchanges two slots and leaves the rest alone. Push moves everything after the target along.',
    hz_ordnen_3: 'Click selects, Shift selects a range, Ctrl+A everything. The bar below shows what you can do with a selection.',
    hz_ordnen_4: 'Ctrl+Z undoes, Ctrl+Y redoes – up to 40 steps back.',
    hz_ordnen_5: 'Ctrl+C puts the selection on the tray, Ctrl+V inserts it. That works in another binder too.',
    hz_foto_t: 'Photograph a binder page', hz_foto_u: 'One photo, and the cards sit in the same order in your slots.',
    hz_foto_1: 'Choose „Capture cards" in the menu and photograph a whole binder page.',
    hz_foto_2: 'Recognition works on the image, not the text – Japanese cards and unreadable numbers included.',
    hz_foto_3: 'The matches are shown side by side for checking; swap anything wrong before you accept.',
    hz_foto_4: 'Costs nothing and runs on our server, not on your phone.',
    hz_drucken_t: 'Print placeholders and lists', hz_drucken_u: 'Black-and-white cards for empty slots, checklist, buy list.',
    hz_drucken_1: '„Print" opens the choice: placeholders, checklist or buy list.',
    hz_drucken_2: 'Placeholders come in real card size (63×88 mm), nine to an A4 sheet, labelled with page and slot.',
    hz_drucken_3: '„Missing only" prints exactly the cards you still need – that is the whole point.',
    hz_drucken_4: 'The buy list comes as CSV for Cardmarket or as a note for your local shop.',
    hz_sammlung_t: 'Keep a collection', hz_sammlung_u: 'What you actually own – separate from the plan, with condition and purchase price.',
    hz_sammlung_1: 'The ✓ in a slot says „got it" and puts the card into your collection.',
    hz_sammlung_2: 'The collection tab holds condition, language, purchase price and grading per copy.',
    hz_sammlung_3: 'Set goals: „set to 100 %" or „every Charizard" – progress follows along.',
    hz_sammlung_4: '„Cheap right now" shows which missing cards currently sit below their average.',
    hz_preise_t: 'Understand the prices', hz_preise_u: 'Where the euro figures come from and what they do not say.',
    hz_preise_1: 'The basis is the Cardmarket trend price in euros, fetched once a day.',
    hz_preise_2: 'Cards without a Cardmarket trend carry a value converted from the US price – that is marked.',
    hz_preise_3: 'The binder value always states how many cards have a price and when it was measured.',
    hz_preise_4: 'Price alert: set a threshold and you hear about it when a card drops below.',
    hz_kunst_t: 'Design art pages', hz_kunst_u: 'A painted page around real cards – and what it costs.',
    hz_kunst_1: 'Choose „Design artwork page" in the page menu while real cards sit on the page.',
    hz_kunst_2: 'Describe what you want and pick a style: watercolour, comic or photo.',
    hz_kunst_3: 'The AI paints around the cards – the slots stay free and the cards fit in.',
    hz_kunst_4: 'One page costs 10 credits; you can print it as often as you like.',
    hz_kunst_5: 'Put into the showcase it earns you credits whenever someone takes it.',
    hz_teilen_t: 'Share a binder', hz_teilen_u: 'Link, QR code, deadline – and how it differs from the showcase.',
    hz_teilen_1: '„Share binder link" in the binder menu opens the dialog.',
    hz_teilen_2: 'Switch on: anyone with the link may watch. No editing, no account.',
    hz_teilen_3: 'The QR code is for the trade table: the person opposite scans and flips along.',
    hz_teilen_4: 'Switching off kills the link but keeps the address – switching it back on is enough.',
    hz_teilen_5: 'The showcase is something else: there the binder stands publicly and gets found.',
    hz_konto_t: 'Account, credits, subscription', hz_konto_u: 'What is free, what Plus and Pro add, how to cancel.',
    hz_konto_1: 'Planning without an account works – it is then saved only in this browser.',
    hz_konto_2: 'Free: 3 binders, 2 placeholder PDFs a month, unlimited checklists.',
    hz_konto_3: 'Plus (€3.99) lifts binders and prints, Pro (€7.99) adds credits for art pages.',
    hz_konto_4: 'Credits are also sold on their own, without a subscription, and they do not expire.',
    hz_konto_5: 'Cancelling: two clicks in your account, or via the cancellation link without signing in.',
